Strata packaged mode: run setup.py and serve/server.py from a read-only tree.

Opt-in: STRATA_STATE_DIR=<writable folder> turns it on; unset, both behave as v0.2.13.
setup.py: STATE_DIR is home() (upstream's seam for where an install writes), so configs, settings.json and the
default data folder (STATE_DIR/data) go there; no scan for other Strata folders, no pip, no engine, reader or
llama.cpp download or compile (engine/strata, its readers and engine/BUILD.json, with a rebuild hint on a GPU or
CPU mismatch; third_party/llama.cpp as installed), no run script, no log file, port 8095 for a new install.
DeepSeek-V4.1 and models of their own shape stop setup: their engines come only from upstream's signed feed.
serve/server.py: a python3 shebang, the config's "port" when no --port is given, an engine with no "log" inherits stderr.
Tests: tools/test_setup_packaged.py, serve/test_packaged.py.  Not sent upstream.

